@page {
    layout: "docs",
    meta: {
        title: "Article blocks",
        description: "Notes, figures, and tabs in Rocdown without raw HTML.",
    },
}

# Article blocks

Use `:name[params]` for bounded documentation components. The parser
stores the kind, params, and body; Rocdown validates the content model;
the theme paints the HTML. Fenced code stays display-only.

:note[title: "Static pages"] {{
    `:note` is legal next to Markdown and `@page` on static site pages.
    `@render` and `@component` belong on hydrate or live pages, not inside
    a `:note` body.
}}

## Note

:caution {{
    Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown. Use a block when the page needs
    structure beyond CommonMark.
}}

## Figure

Nested `:img` owns the accessible name. `caption` and `credit` are
optional labels around that image.

:figure[caption: "The Rocci stack"] {{
    :img[src: "/assets/diagrams/stack.svg", alt: "Roc and Datastar sit under templates, applications, and Rocdown.", loading: "lazy", decoding: "async"]
}}

Meaningful images require `alt`. Set `decorative: True` only when the
image is purely decorative.

## Tabs

Every tab panel is in the document. Print, forced-colors, and browsers
with scripts disabled show all panels. `:tabs` bodies may contain only
`:tab` children.

:tabs.begin[group: "docs-check", kind: "tool"]
    :tab[id: "check", label: "Check"] {{
        Validate the catalog without compiling Roc:

        ```sh
        rocdown check docs
        ```
    }}
    :tab[id: "build", label: "Build"] {{
        Write the static tree:

        ```sh
        rocdown build docs
        ```
    }}
:tabs.end

Params go in `[]`. Content is the rest of the line, `{{ }}`, or
`:kind.begin` … `:kind.end`. Do not mix `.begin` with double braces on
the same call.

The other kinds (`:steps`, `:include`, `:badge`, `:file-tree`,
`:example`, …) are in the
[language reference](/docs/rocdown/language/). Custom painters belong in
the compiled theme, not `@use`, on a static site.

Next: [Sites](/docs/rocdown/sites/).
